{"action_id":null,"arguments":[],"assumptions":[{"assumption_id":"node.202b853856b53f0bb20eae12.a0","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The selected control tests Q3's stated licensing trigger, not licence possession, unlawful unlicensed conduct or overall legal compliance.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.202b853856b53f0bb20eae12.a1","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Any applicable regulated-activity carve-out has been resolved before supplying regulated_services; exclusion from Type 9 does not itself exclude another regulated activity.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.202b853856b53f0bb20eae12.a2","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The three facts concern the same office, services, business and assessment circumstances.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.202b853856b53f0bb20eae12.a3","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The conjunction represents the stated trigger within this selected control, not an exhaustive account of obligations under absent governing provisions.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.202b853856b53f0bb20eae12.a4","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Qualified ordinary-course guidance informs services_as_business without assigning it automatically from expense reimbursement or profit purpose.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.202b853856b53f0bb20eae12.a5","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The supplied text is interpreted as retained evidence; legal authenticity and current authority are not inferred from its locator.","status":"PROVISIONAL"}],"bundle_hash":"9e5477060c16744466dfe98a258c0cafdc3b1055f8032470440ffedc99f3d199","candidate_id":"candidate.94b4eea143f040c980e5fa7e3d2519ec","controlled_language":"[TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT] For the selected Q3 trigger control only, true means all three stated trigger conditions are satisfied after upstream carve-outs: regulated services, business provision of those services, and that business being carried on in Hong Kong. The tag denotes satisfaction of the trigger predicate, not compliance with a licensing obligation. Exceptions attach to the relevant classifications rather than supplying an additional blanket exemption. Unknown classifications remain unknown.","disposition_reason":"Unreviewed interpretation proposal","family_ids":["exceptions"],"generation_phase":"SHARED_RESOLUTION","issue_ids":["issue.c9abbeac88cc4c9c91409617b08b7d91","issue.f7e0b34bb098403f8fd20de7bda99c9f","issue.d95aaa5e34924cbc9e9359df5eb0089b","issue.ea739dfb08694fffba93dbd558bc9e8d","issue.cd4a315a3de644f69547036ba04f2bfd","issue.4f0ba4e9e2ca4db0a1f959c7700a22f4"],"parent_id":"candidate.6505eba874794d4f8e97a958fd63cb13","probability_of_legal_correctness":null,"revision_reason":"Retain local exception attachment: Type 9 exclusion affects regulated_services; ordinary-course guidance affects services_as_business; expense reimbursement qualifies only the no-income description within that guidance. The rival hypothesis of a separate blanket family-office exemption fails because the text anchors these qualifications to particular classifications and preserves ordinary-course modality. It could wrongly negate a trigger involving another regulated activity or exceptional business circumstances. The unresolved negation in the business/profit phrase may materially alter business classification, but does not justify inventing a second trigger formula. Both absence-of-business-and-profit and a narrower reach of negation remain grammatical questions, not approved Boolean alternatives. The supplied diagnostics contain no fact-bound counterexample with which to distinguish them.","run_id":"run.98deff83a1104c269f71172a12f08a93","scheduling_priority":0,"schema_version":"interpretation.v1","score_purpose":"INVESTIGATION_PRIORITY_ONLY","source_packet_hash":"e7c3a71dc77ad1426f9f9ab7bc8f5b31438bca655a186478fa311d88d3e866ae","source_unit_ids":["daa1876316641.u38.27681","daa1876316641.u39.28171","daa1876316641.u40.28601","daa1876316641.u53.30093","daa1876316641.u6